{"id":"neet-2018-q006","pn":6,"y":"NEET 2018 · 6 May","tp":"Semiconductor Electronics","st":"Transistor as amplifier circuit","q":"In the circuit shown in the figure, the input voltage Vi is 20 V, VBE = 0 and VCE = 0. The values of IB, IC and β are given by","o":["IB = 40 µA, IC = 10 mA, β = 250","IB = 25 µA, IC = 5 mA, β = 200","IB = 20 µA, IC = 5 mA, β = 250","IB = 40 µA, IC = 5 mA, β = 125"],"c":3,"s":"Input loop: 20 – IB × 500 × 10³ – VBE = 0, with VBE = 0.\nIB = (20)/(5 × 10⁵) = 4 × 10⁻⁵ A = 40 µA.\nOutput loop: 20 – IC × 4 × 10³ – VCE = 0, with VCE = 0.\nIC = (20)/(4 × 10³) = 5 mA.\nβ = (IC)/(IB) = (5 × 10⁻³)/(40 × 10⁻⁶) = 125.","fig":{"w":260,"h":190,"alt":"Common-emitter n-p-n transistor: 20 V supply through RC = 4 kΩ to the collector, input Vi through RB = 500 kΩ to the base, emitter grounded.","d":[["c",150,105,22,""],["l",139,92,139,118,""],["l",139,100,110,100,""],["l",139,98,155,84,""],["l",155,84,155,63,""],["l",139,110,154,123,"a"],["l",155,123,155,150,""],["p","M155 28L155 32.4L150 34.6L160 38.9L150 43.3L160 47.7L150 52.1L160 56.4L155 58.6L155 63",""],["c",155,24,2.6,"F"],["l",155,150,155,150,""],["l",155,150,155,158,""],["l",146,158,164,158,""],["l",149,162,161,162,""],["l",152,166,158,166,""],["t",155,14,"20V","m"],["t",165,86,"C","s"],["t",160,136,"E","s"],["t",121,120,"B","s"],["l",139,92,139,118,"B"],["c",40,100,2.6,"F"],["l",40,100,66,100,""],["p","M66 100L71 100L73.5 96L78.5 104L83.5 96L88.5 104L93.5 96L98.5 104L101 100L106 100",""],["l",106,100,139,100,""],["t",34,104,"Vᵢ","e"],["t",88,88,"R","e"],["t",89,91,"B","s"],["t",86,118,"500 kΩ","m"],["t",131,50,"R","e"],["t",132,53,"C","s"],["t",165,50,"4 kΩ",""]]},"sfig":{"w":260,"h":190,"alt":"The same circuit with the base current IB marked on the input side and loops drawn for the input and output sides.","d":[["c",150,105,22,""],["l",139,92,139,118,""],["l",139,100,110,100,""],["l",139,98,155,84,""],["l",155,84,155,63,""],["l",139,110,154,123,"a"],["l",155,123,155,150,""],["p","M155 28L155 32.4L150 34.6L160 38.9L150 43.3L160 47.7L150 52.1L160 56.4L155 58.6L155 63",""],["c",155,24,2.6,"F"],["l",155,150,155,150,""],["l",155,150,155,158,""],["l",146,158,164,158,""],["l",149,162,161,162,""],["l",152,166,158,166,""],["t",155,14,"20V","m"],["t",165,86,"C","s"],["t",160,136,"E","s"],["t",121,120,"B","s"],["l",139,92,139,118,"B"],["c",40,100,2.6,"F"],["l",40,100,66,100,""],["p","M66 100L71 100L73.5 96L78.5 104L83.5 96L88.5 104L93.5 96L98.5 104L101 100L106 100",""],["l",106,100,139,100,""],["l",48,88,100,88,"a"],["t",72,80,"I","e"],["t",73,83,"B","s"],["t",4,130,"Vᵢ = 20V",""],["t",90,118,"500 kΩ","m"],["p","M52 140C82 140 108 152 120 178","a"],["l",200,40,200,168,"a"]]}},
{"id":"neet-2018-q007","pn":7,"y":"NEET 2018 · 6 May","tp":"Semiconductor Electronics","st":"p-n junction diode characteristics","q":"In a p-n junction diode, change in temperature due to heating","o":["affects only reverse resistance","affects only forward resistance","does not affect resistance of p-n junction","affects the overall V – I characteristics of p-n junction"],"c":3,"s":"The diode current is I = I₀(e^(qV/kT) – 1).\nBoth I₀ and the exponent depend on temperature T.\nSo heating changes both forward and reverse behaviour, that is the whole V–I characteristic."}
